# Session and video UI legibility

Sessions are recorded in **presenter mode** and published on **YouTube (1080p)**. Every user-visible label, body line, code bubble, and control must read **at a glance on a TV-sized stream** — not just on a laptop at arm's length.

**Default assumption: you are designing a slide, not a dense app UI.**

If in doubt between two sizes — always pick the **larger** one. Fewer words at larger size beats more words at small size.

## Typography — hard minimums (never go below)

| Role | Tailwind floor | Preferred on full-slide panels |
|---|---|---|
| In-component headings (`h2`/`h3`) | `text-xl md:text-2xl` | `text-2xl md:text-3xl` |
| Body / explanations / step detail | `text-lg md:text-xl` | `text-xl md:text-2xl` |
| Section labels ("USER INPUT", "TOKENS", etc.) | `text-base md:text-lg` | `text-lg md:text-xl` — always `font-bold` |
| API / JSON / monospace payloads | `text-base md:text-lg` | `text-lg md:text-xl` in hero code bubbles |
| Buttons / toggles / step controls | `text-base md:text-lg` | `py-3 px-5` minimum tap target |
| Secondary / hint copy | `text-base` | Never use `text-sm` even for hints |

## Absolutely banned — zero exceptions

- `text-xs` anywhere in teaching UI
- `text-sm` as primary or secondary teaching copy
- Arbitrary small sizes: `text-[10px]`, `text-[11px]`, `text-[12px]`, `text-[13px]`
- Faint labels on dark shells: `text-gray-500` or dimmer for anything the presenter reads aloud
- Wrapping long explanations into tiny condensed pills just to fit more on one slide — **split into a new slide instead**

## Contrast requirements

- **Dark shells:** body text `text-gray-100`–`text-gray-200`; secondary text minimum `text-gray-300`
- **Light shells:** body text `text-gray-800`–`text-gray-900`; secondary minimum `text-gray-600`
- Never rely on color alone to distinguish active vs inactive states — use size or weight too

## Blocks and spacing

- **Outer panels:** `p-8 md:p-10` for full-slide interactives; `space-y-6`–`space-y-10` between major blocks
- **Inner cards:** `p-5 md:p-6` minimum
- **Chips / pills:** `py-3 px-4` minimum; hero rows `text-lg md:text-2xl` with `ring-1` or border for separation on video
- Do not shrink padding to fit more content — remove content instead

## SVG and diagrams

- All SVG label text: **16px+ in user units** (equivalent to `text-base` or larger)
- Avoid 9–10px axis labels; only tick marks may be that small, and only when the axis label above them is large
- Node labels, edge labels, step names inside SVGs: 16px+ minimum; 18–20px preferred

## Enforcement on new and edited components

- Any **new** session-facing component must meet this rule from the very first commit
- When editing an existing component, **upgrade all typography in that component** to meet these minimums — do not leave old small text alongside new large text
- Non-user-facing code (`lib/`, types, tests) is exempt, but do not re-export tiny UI from shared session barrels
